CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "ab04d749-0a82-40c2-9a6c-22bcd0ab5c9a",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T21:41:39Z",
  "ticket_id": "86c8-2d40",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "A FILE_IMPACT event type is supported by the ticket system: ticket-lib.sh write_commit_event() accepts FILE_IMPACT in its event type enum, and ticket-reducer.py compiles FILE_IMPACT events into a structured file_impact field in the ticket's compiled state \u2014 containing an array of {path, reason} objects with latest-wins semantics",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (FILE_IMPACT event support) that persists after implementation, phrased as ongoing behavior of the system"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "ticket set-file-impact <id> <json> stores structured file impact data as a FILE_IMPACT event; ticket get-file-impact <id> returns the structured array; ticket show <id> includes the file_impact field in its output",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capabilities for storing and retrieving file impact data that persist after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The Jira outbound bridge surfaces file impact in Jira using two mechanisms: (a) a Jira issue property (key: dso.file_impact, set via direct REST API PUT to /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/properties/dso.file_impact using AcliClient._direct_rest_put() \u2014 a new method justified by spike confirming ACLI has no properties subcommand) for machine-readable storage, and (b) a single formatted comment (deduped by UUID marker via the existing comment dedup mechanism and .jira-comment-map) for human visibility. The inbound bridge ignores the dso.file_impact property (properties live outside fields.*) and deduplicates the outbound comment via the existing dedup map. Bridge auth: if API token, no scope change required; if OAuth 2.0, confirm write:jira-work scope is present",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (how the bridge surfaces file impact) rather than a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "bridge-outbound.py process_outbound() handles FILE_IMPACT events explicitly \u2014 they do not fall through silently. When issue property PUT fails, a BRIDGE_ALERT event is written with reason FILE_IMPACT_SYNC_FAILED; when comment add fails, a distinct BRIDGE_ALERT event is written with reason FILE_IMPACT_COMMENT_SYNC_FAILED; no transactional rollback across the two channels",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior where the process_outbound() function explicitly handles FILE_IMPACT events with specific alert mechanisms, a property that remains true after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "update-artifacts.sh is extended with a data migration phase: the first registered migration scans all tickets for ## File Impact patterns in COMMENT event bodies and description text, extracts file paths, and writes corresponding FILE_IMPACT events. Success: all tickets with parseable patterns have a FILE_IMPACT event; unparseable tickets logged to stderr with ticket ID and skipped; re-running on migrated tickets is a no-op (stamp prevents re-run, keyed by migration ID file-impact-v1). Stamp records {version, migrated_at, tickets_processed, tickets_skipped}. Test suite includes well-formed fixture, malformed fixture, and idempotency case",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time data migration task with completion criteria, idempotency safeguards, and logging of processed/skipped counts"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "enrich-file-impact.sh is refactored: LLM generation (Haiku API call) stays in the workflow layer; storage changes from ticket comment to ticket set-file-impact. sprint-drift-check.sh and sprint-review-scope-check.sh are also refactored to use ticket get-file-impact instead of ad-hoc markdown parsing \u2014 all four ad-hoc parsers migrate to the structured API. Markdown parsers preserved as SECONDARY fallback for tickets pre-migration",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes the durable architectural outcome where the system uses structured API calls with markdown parsing as a secondary fallback, not a one-time completion event"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
